  "articleBody": "Getting ready to hang new drywall means thinking through your space from framing to final coat. Here is a clear guide to help you plan properly.\n\nOverview\nHanging drywall turns open framing into clean, functional rooms. Done right, it creates smooth walls that last for years.\n\nKey Benefits\nProper installation prevents future seam cracks, hides framing imperfections, and delivers the exact surface finish your paint needs.\n\nProcess Breakdown\n- Assess framing: Check studs and joists for plumb lines and level planes before a single board goes up.\n- Plan sheet layout: Use the longest practical panels to minimize butt joints and keep edges loosely butted.\n- Fasten with care: Drive screws just below the paper surface without puncturing or tearing it.\n- Tape, mud, and sand: Apply compound in multiple thin coats, allowing complete drying time between applications before final sanding and primer.\n\nReal Examples\nBasement build-outs and open-concept additions benefit from careful board orientation to prevent visible seams under bright lighting.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start\nCheck whether insulation, rough electrical, and plumbing runs have passed any needed inspections. Confirm ceiling heights so your installer orders the right board lengths.\n\nReady to hang new drywall on your project? Call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to talk through your job.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
